.TH "YAMLR-INTEGRATIONS" "1" "May 2026" "Yamlr Manual" "User Commands"
.SH "NAME"
yamlr-integrations \- Propose repairs and remediate Kubernetes manifests.
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
\fBCI/CD Template Marketplace\fR
.PP
The \fByamlr integrations\fR command provides production-ready CI/CD templates to bridge the gap between local manifest auditing and automated pipeline enforcement.
.PP
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.nf
.RS
# Export GitLab CI template
yamlr integrations gitlab

# Export Jenkins Pipeline snippet
yamlr integrations jenkins
.RE
.fi
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
To ensure "Zero-Touch" adoption in large organizations, Yamlr provides opinionated integration templates. These templates are optimized for:
.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fBPerformance\fR: Leveraging caching and shallow cloning where possible.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fBObservability\fR: Standardized SARIF output for GitHub/GitLab security dashboards.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fBSafety\fR: Enabling strict GitOps gates that block deployments on critical safety regressions.
.SH "SUPPORTED PLATFORMS"
.SS "1. GitLab CI (`gitlab`)"
Generates a \fB.gitlab-ci.yml\fR job definition that can be included in your main pipeline.
.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fBFeatures\fR: Merge Request security reports, code quality artifacts, and pipeline badges.
.SS "2. Jenkins (`jenkins`)"
Generates a \fBJenkinsfile\fR stage snippet compatible with modern Pipeline-as-Code.
.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fBFeatures\fR: Specialized pipeline steps for \fByamlr scan\fR and \fByamlr heal --dry-run\fR to provide feedback to developers.
.SH "EXAMPLES"
.SS "GitLab CI Integration"
.nf
.RS
yamlr integrations gitlab > .yamlr-ci.yml
.RE
.fi
Then include it in your \fB.gitlab-ci.yml\fR:
.PP
.nf
.RS
include:
  - local: '.yamlr-ci.yml'
.RE
.fi
---
.PP
.IP "\fBNOTE:\fR" 4
This command is part of the \fBYamlr Ecosystem\fR and is available in the Free version to encourage best-practice GitOps adoption.
.PP
